{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>Some say הכצעקתה means \"the outcry that has come to Me.\"</b> If so, what they have done — I will do destruction upon them." "<b>And if not, I will know.</b> I will have compassion on them. So too they interpret וידע אלהים (Exodus 2:25). In my opinion its meaning is: I will see whether they have all done like this grass, for the truth is that He knows every particular in a general way, and not in a particular way. And the proof that this interpretation is the truth — and if it is a great sod that Abraham said האף תספה — is that the he of האף is opened, and if it is for metonymy because of the alef, which is from the throat, for the rule of the holy tongue is to widen that which comes before it."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {1 "The final clause is compressed and elliptical; rendered hyper-literally. The argument turns on Hebrew phonology (the open syllable before a guttural) but is stated with extreme brevity and no connective explanation."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:45:02.355886910Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}